Third-party code in src/port/xtensa
===================================

This folder is for Xtensa cores, among them Espressif's ESP32 (LX6),
ESP32-S2 and ESP32-S3 (LX7), in the windowed register ABI or call0. The
ESP32-C, H and P series are RISC-V, and use src/port/riscv32.

The three files listed below come from newlib, copied byte for byte and
never edited. Each carries Tensilica's notice, the MIT licence in full.
Espressif's newlib-esp32 holds the same bytes. The other files in this
folder belong to libterae and are under libterae's licence, given at the
top of each: port_memcpy.S and port_memset.S, which are the files
assembled, port_memmove.c and port_memcmp.c, and xtensa/config/core-isa.h,
which stands in for the core's configuration header and says what it sets.

This folder is checked by building it, with src/, with Espressif's GCC: see
"What is checked" below.


